{
  "title": "Arshad Warsi Joins Shah Rukh Khan's 'King' Cast",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-18T16:36:42+05:30",
  "summary": "Actor Arshad Warsi has reportedly joined the cast of Shah Rukh Khan's upcoming film 'King', which marks the big screen debut of Khan's daughter Suhana Khan. The film, directed by Siddharth Anand of 'Pathaan' fame, will feature Warsi in a pivotal role though character details remain under wraps.",
  "content": "Shah Rukh Khan's upcoming film 'King' has been generating significant buzz since its initial announcement last year. The project gains additional attention as it's directed by Siddharth Anand, who helmed Khan's comeback film 'Pathaan', and marks the theatrical debut of Shah Rukh's daughter Suhana Khan following her OTT debut in 'The Archies'.\n\nAccording to a report by Peeping Moon, Arshad Warsi has joined the film's cast in a pivotal role, though specific details about his character are currently confidential. While Shah Rukh Khan and Warsi have maintained a long-standing friendship, this marks their first substantial collaboration in a film together, aside from Khan's previous guest appearance in Warsi's 2005 film 'Kuchh Meetha Ho Jayein'.\n\nThe film is being produced under Khan's Red Chillies Entertainment and Siddharth Anand's Marflix Pictures. The cast also includes notable actors Abhishek Bachchan and Abhay Verma of 'Munjya' fame.",
